# Snap packages for every host that has snapd (one per line).
# Installed by: setup/modules/21-snap.sh (skipped where snapd is absent)
# Docs:         docs/reference/package-managers.md
#
# Format: NAME [--install-opt..] [plug..]
#   --classic, --channel=…  passed to `snap install`
#   any other word          a plug to connect as NAME:plug
#
# Snap is the last resort: only what has no reasonable apt or flatpak package.

# Process/system monitor, first choice for PROCVIEWER (.common_env). apt only
# has btm 0.10.x and there is no flatpak. Without these plugs it shows partial
# data and cannot signal processes. Runs via bin/bottom (XDG workaround).
bottom system-observe process-control hardware-observe mount-observe
